    "methods_description": "Participants performed an orientation memory task with color-cued predictability manipulation. Memory items were preceded by central color cues (red, green, or blue). In predictive trials, two colors cued non-overlapping 90° orientation segments, constraining possible item orientations. In non-predictive trials, a third color signaled unconstrained orientations. Participants judged whether probe gratings were rotated clockwise or counterclockwise relative to memorized orientations.",
